      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like these conversions don\u0027t change anything. mm/madvise.c opts into `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e` since aosp/4312489, so `PAGE_SIZE` here is already `mm_pte_size(p3s_current_mm())`, and MADV_FREE only ever runs on `current-\u003emm`: madvise() passes it, process_madvise() rejects MADV_FREE for another mm in process_madvise_remote_valid() (and vector_madvise() enters the target\u0027s context with `P3S_CONTEXT_REMOTE_MM()` anyway), and io_uring, with `IORING_OP_MADVISE`, is disabled in 4KB processes since aosp/4368076. So `tlb-\u003emm` is always `p3s_current_mm()` in madvise_free_pte_range().\n\nWould it be OK to drop this patch? The re-indent of the madvise_folio_pte_batch() call fixes the continuation line that aosp/4367604 wrapped, so it could be folded there.",
